  "note": "The five v3 registrars, started on 20 Nov 2026 between 11:19 and 11:23 UTC next to the five v2.1 registrars, which were not touched (same containers, same uptime, no log line during the step). Each one registered its enclave on the v3 EnclaveRegistry, the chain checking Intel's signature through DCAP, then bound it to its machine on the v3 MachineRegistry (PPID read from Intel's certificate in the quote). The first one (product 2) also submitted the Proof of Cloud alliance's token for the machine to the v3 ProofOfCloudAuditor, so product 5 meets its verified-level policy. They were started one at a time, each after the previous one's first pass and only when the operator had no pending transaction (the key is shared with the v2.1 registrars): nonces 190 to 200, no collision. Since then they renew before each window ends (4 h before) and keep the binding and the token up to date; products 1 and 3 also settle what their enclaves serve (sessions, x402 calls).",
